    {
      "id": 185506,
      "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
      "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-11-29T03:18:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Kratos13\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/65b543/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Kratos13:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I assume Resolute-&gt;Prayer of Desperation follows the same guidelines as Don't Dismiss Anything-&gt;Know When to Hold Fast, which was ruled in the Fireside Chat as DDA allowing to finish before ending the turn.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's not quite accurate. &nbsp;The turn \"ends\" and then DDA finishes. &nbsp;The trick is that \"End your turn\" means \"Move to the beginning of your End of Turn step\", and does not actually mean your turn is over. &nbsp;That's why \"end your turn\" cards become hilarious when Wager Master's card that reverses the order of a turn is out, because \"end your turn\" moves you to the End of Turn step, which is now the beginning of your turn and you get power and play phases again.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:11:01.860Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.2,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 15887,
      "topic_slug": "resolute-prayer-of-desperation",
      "display_username": "Arcanist Lupus",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"Kratos13\"]\n\nI assume Resolute-&gt;Prayer of Desperation follows the same guidelines as Don&#39;t Dismiss Anything-&gt;Know When to Hold Fast, which was ruled in the Fireside Chat as DDA allowing to finish before ending the turn.\n\n[/quote]\n\nThat&#39;s not quite accurate. &nbsp;The turn &quot;ends&quot; and then DDA finishes. &nbsp;The trick is that &quot;End your turn&quot; means &quot;Move to the beginning of your End of Turn step&quot;, and does not actually mean your turn is over. &nbsp;That&#39;s why &quot;end your turn&quot; cards become hilarious when Wager Master&#39;s card that reverses the order of a turn is out, because &quot;end your turn&quot; moves you to the End of Turn step, which is now the beginning of your turn and you get power and play phases again.\n",
